id: 4-2-airship
name: WORLD 4-2
world: 4
stage: 2
;; theme: airship-deck once A3's theme is registered (castle until then)
theme: castle
music: airship
time: inherit
start: 2,6
startMode: stand
;; SMB3 auto-scroll (A1); until it lands the camera scrolls normally (`camera: scroll`)
camera: auto
scroll: 0.375
parent: 4-2

;; Larry Koopa's airship, the deck (0.5.0), laid out after SMB3 World 1's airship (owner's
;; reference), all art and music original. The camera scrolls on its own (0.375 px/f: about
;; 57 s from the bow to the stern) and stops at the stern.
;; - BOW (0-32): a raised bow platform (row 7, the start) over the stair-stepped prow, the fore
;;   deck (row 9) with two cannons aimed up-left (14, 22), a Rocky Wrench manhole (18), a short
;;   post with a Bullet Bill blaster at its right end (26-28) and the tall post (31-32, 3 high)
;;   where the deck steps down. A propeller turns under the prow's bottom hull (23).
;; - MIDDLE (33-70): the long low main deck (row 12) on two hull segments with a 2-wide gap
;;   (50-51), a propeller under each (40, 61); a blaster post (44), a plain post (59) and a ?
;;   block (53, mushroom, or fire flower when big). Above it the plank overhang (row 3, 40-60)
;;   with cannons hanging under it aimed down (43 dl, 49 dr), a four-cannon turret (56-57), and
;;   at its right end the thick block (61-75, rows 3-5) over the metal gateway (61-68, not solid)
;;   with one more cannon hanging under it (72).
;; - STERN (71-95): the lower deck (row 13) with a Rocky Wrench (75), a cannon (79) and a blaster
;;   (82), then steps up (85-88) to the high stern deck (row 8, 89-95): a railing, portholes in
;;   the hull, a propeller under it, and THE PIPE (92) down into Larry's room (4-2-larry).
;; Cannon cells are solid (the cannon fills its own cell). Every gap is 2 wide and every step up
;; at most 2 tiles from where the hero can stand, except the tall post (3 above the fore deck,
;; 2 above the blaster post next to it); tests/sim/airship-deck.test.ts runs every hero across.
